{"name":"Plantain Chips","hex":"#d6a550","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plantain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the genus Plantago, with a rosette of sessile leaves about 10 cm (4\") long with a narrow part instead of a petiole, and with a spike inflorescence with the flower spacing varying widely among the species. See also psyllium."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant in the genus Musa, the genus that includes banana, but with lower sugar content than banana.","The fruit of the plant, usually cooked before eating and used like potatoes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plantain"},{"term":"chips","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of chip"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of chip","Money."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chips"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fried plantain","blocks":[{"text":"Fried plantain is a dish cooked wherever plantains grow, from West Africa to East Africa as well as Central America, the tropical region of northern South America and the Caribbean countries such as Haiti and Cuba and in many parts of Southeast Asia and Oceania, where fried snacks are widely popular. In Indonesia, it is called pisang goreng. It is called dodo in Yoruba in South West Nigeria, otherwise known as simply fried plantain in other parts of Nigeria. Kelewele is a fried spicy plantain typically served as a side dish for red red and fish stew in Ghana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Vendeuses_de_bananes_plantain.jpg/330px-Vendeuses_de_bananes_plantain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fried_plantain","wikidata":"Q5503628"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Aloko.jpg/500px-Aloko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"